  "testament": "old",
  "chapter": 10,
  "sortOrder": 19010,
  "verseCount": 18,
  "aliases": [
    "Psalm",
    "Psalms",
    "Ps",
    "Psa",
    "Psm"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:10:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Why standest thou afar off, O LORD? why hidest thou thyself in times of trouble?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 10:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:10:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:10:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "The wicked in his pride doth persecute the poor: let them be taken in the devices that they have imagined.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 10:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:10:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:10:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "For the wicked boasteth of his heart’s desire, and blesseth the covetous, whom the LORD abhorreth.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 10:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:10:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:10:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "The wicked, through the pride of his countenance, will not seek after God: God is not in all his thoughts.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 10:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:10:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:10:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "His ways are always grievous; thy judgments are far above out of his sight: as for all his enemies, he puffeth at them.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 10:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:10:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:10:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "He hath said in his heart, I shall not be moved: for I shall never be in adversity.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 10:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:10:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:10:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "His mouth is full of cursing and deceit and fraud: under his tongue is mischief and vanity.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 10:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:10:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:10:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "He sitteth in the lurking places of the villages: in the secret places doth he murder the innocent: his eyes are privily set against the poor.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 10:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:10:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:10:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "He lieth in wait secretly as a lion in his den: he lieth in wait to catch the poor: he doth catch the poor, when he draweth him into his net.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 10:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:10:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:10:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "He croucheth, and humbleth himself, that the poor may fall by his strong ones.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 10:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:10:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:10:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "He hath said in his heart, God hath forgotten: he hideth his face; he will never see it.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 10:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:10:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:10:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "Arise, O LORD; O God, lift up thine hand: forget not the humble.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 10:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:10:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:10:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "Wherefore doth the wicked contemn God? he hath said in his heart, Thou wilt not require it.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 10:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:10:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:10:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "Thou hast seen it; for thou beholdest mischief and spite, to requite it with thy hand: the poor committeth himself unto thee; thou art the helper of the fatherless.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 10:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:10:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:10:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "Break thou the arm of the wicked and the evil man: seek out his wickedness till thou find none.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 10:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:10:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:10:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "The LORD is King for ever and ever: the heathen are perished out of his land.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 10:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:10:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:10:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "LORD, thou hast heard the desire of the humble: thou wilt prepare their heart, thou wilt cause thine ear to hear:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 10:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:10:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:10:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "To judge the fatherless and the oppressed, that the man of the earth may no more oppress.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 10:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:10:18"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
